# Local vector response milestone

The target is a local positive-field-energy realization, for every constant
0<D<=N, alpha>0, G>0 and unit e in three spatial dimensions, of scalar static
susceptibility (N k_perp²+D k_parallel²)/k^4. A full tensor inverse, local flux
bound and normalized retarded distribution are required. Agreement on axes,
finite numerical sampling, group speed, or a fitted response alone is not closure.
The isotropic limit, k=0 distributional limit, point-source singularity and
D approaching zero are explicit boundary cases.

The parent directly authored the construction within the observations-to-TOE
campaign. Its fixed end is 2026-10-13T16:53:00.057432Z; this milestone creates
no new clock. Current-main source is516cb69d8487ff04f8a48e065d3dcbe71d7dd237;
standing instruction source is3a4b2c66a1ead7a1c48b4359627e968f681e3c39.

The standalone canonical note contains every load-bearing hypothesis and proof.
The campaign's direct_vector_response_completion packet preserves original
source, prior motivating constrained dynamics, controls and independent checks.
That provenance supplies no hidden empirical input to the canonical theorem.
